# Generated from: specs/441-continue-an-explicit-execute-queue-after-the-previous-issue-is-delivered/requirements.md
Feature: Continue an explicit execute queue after the previous issue is delivered
  Delivery left the checkout on the delivered issue branch,
  so the next queued issue stopped with active_issue_conflict.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Queue continues after a delivered issue
    Given an explicit queue of issues 42 and 43 started from the default branch
    When issue 42 is MERGED at its head and CLOSED
    Then the controller switches to the default branch and processes issue 43

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Undelivered or dirty foreign branches still fail closed
    Given the checkout is on issue 42's branch that is not delivered or has changes outside .omp
    When issue 43 is processed
    Then the controller stops with active_issue_conflict and preserves the branch and worktree
